- description: This metric evaluates the presence and completeness of docstrings within functions and classes in a codebase. It measures the proportion of functions and classes that have associated documentation, as well as the quality of that documentation, which includes clarity, conciseness, and relevance. The scope encompasses all public and private methods and classes, ensuring that both user-facing and internal components are adequately documented. Missing or incomplete docstrings are flagged, highlighting areas where additional documentation is necessary to improve code understandability. This metric is crucial for maintaining high standards of code quality and facilitating collaboration among developers.

