- description: This metric evaluates the existence and quality of test files within a code repository, providing insights into the robustness of the testing practices employed. It measures the presence of unit, integration, and end-to-end tests, as well as the overall coverage of the codebase by these tests. The metric also considers the organization and clarity of the test files, which can impact maintainability and ease of understanding for future developers. By assessing these factors, the metric helps identify potential gaps in testing that could lead to undetected bugs or issues in the software. Ultimately, it serves as an indicator of the reliability and stability of the codebase, reflecting the commitment to quality assurance in the development process.

