- description: This metric evaluates the quality and consistency of feature engineering code used in machine learning workflows. It specifically measures the reproducibility of features generated during the training phase and ensures that the same features are available during model serving. The scope includes assessing the alignment of feature transformations, encoding methods, and any preprocessing steps applied to the data. Typical signals include discrepancies in feature values or types between training datasets and production environments. This metric is crucial for maintaining model performance and reliability, as inconsistencies can lead to degraded predictions and unexpected behavior in deployed models.

