- description: This metric evaluates the setup and execution of hyperparameter tuning processes, specifically focusing on frameworks such as Optuna and Ray Tune. It measures the effectiveness of the tuning strategy by assessing the reproducibility of the results, ensuring that the same hyperparameter configurations yield consistent model performance across different runs. Additionally, the metric examines the persistence of the best configurations, verifying that optimal hyperparameters are documented and can be reliably retrieved for future use. The scope includes both the methodology employed for tuning and the management of hyperparameter configurations throughout the machine learning lifecycle. This metric is crucial for maintaining high standards in model training and deployment, as it directly impacts the reliability and efficiency of machine learning workflows.

